{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
  "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Credit Suisse Securities)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The pivotal question in this case is whether this Court's decisions in Gordon and NASD require implied antitrust immunity as the district court believed. And we submit that the answer is yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did we mention them in those cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (as amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States has responsibility for enforcing both the securities laws through the SEC and the antitrust laws through the Justice Department and the FTC. It thus has a critical interest in ensuring that these laws can be reconciled in a manner that gives effect to both, and completely ousts neither."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask this question about the laddering and so forth? If it were fully disclosed, would it be unlawful under either statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In light of the very fine line, how is the Court to distinguish between -- determine whether what's alleged is inextricably intertwined with authorized conduct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And even then, why do you take the other position? It is pretty easy to imagine the SEC, under some circumstances, deciding that's a proper way to market securities, to have some kinds of agreements between IPOs or something like that. I don't see why not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you if your conspiracy allegation would be the same if there were only one underwriter?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So what's at issue here is not whether you get a remedy. It's whether you get treble damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why is that? I don't understand why the SEC could not -- they can make rules for a single IPO; it seems to me they can make rules for coordination of IPO. Why can't they do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. LOVELL",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LOVELL: They agreed to inflate prices in precisely the way the securities laws have always prohibited."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How could the Court -- how could a court enforce that at the 12(b)(6) stage?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: We all agree, say a group of underwriters, that for the next we will insist that every customer, whatever price we charge, will pay 30 percent more for 50 percent more shares next month. Absolutely illegal, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAPIRO: The same circumstances were presented very similar to the NASD in the Invemed case. They had a Three-week trial, 17 experts, and they concluded that those charges were quite permissible considering the whole range of services that were given."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, if this occurred with concerted action the SEC has power to deal with concerted action. Congress said that they could deal with multiple party manipulations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1157",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0393be30f0b98f9868e24c23478cf444fd3b111a5d668e3a4e066c24811c2923",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0393be30f0b9-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is now submitted."
    },
    {
